{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[B]You have heard and read about the [E]state of [B]Tennessee
[B]Down in the southern states is [C#7]where I want to [F#7]be
Where the [B]valleys are so green And the [E]mountains are so [B]tall
[B]You will know just what I mean [F#]When you hear them say “you [B]all”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Tennessee [E](Tennessee)
I hear you calling [B]me (I hear you calling me)
[B]The home of Davey Crockett in the [F#]hills of [B]Tennessee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When I was a little boy around the folks back home
My mother always said to me, "Jimmy, please don't roam"
Now that I have strayed away, my heart is full of woe
When I think of mom and dad, that's where I want to go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
If ever I get back to the state of Tennessee
I tell you there'll be no more roaming for me
There lives a sweetheart who said she'd marry me
As soon as I get back to the state of Tennessee
{end_of_chorus}
